subtasks.description:
Implement the ClassifierBudgetGuard policy and integrate it into the classifier spawning flow.

**Part 1: classifier_budget_guard.go** — Replace the stub Evaluate with real logic:

```go
func (g *ClassifierBudgetGuard) Evaluate(task *model.Task) ClassifierBudgetAction {
    if task.Context == nil {
        task.Context = make(model.JSONField)
    }
    maxSpawns := g.MaxSpawns
    if maxSpawns == 0 {
        maxSpawns = DefaultMaxClassifierSpawns
    }
    counter, _ := task.Context[classifierSpawnCounterKey].(float64)
    counter++
    task.Context[classifierSpawnCounterKey] = counter
    if int(counter) > maxSpawns {
        return ClassifierFail
    }
    return ClassifierContinue
}
```

Constants: `DefaultMaxClassifierSpawns = 2`, `classifierSpawnCounterKey = "total_classifier_spawns"`.

**Part 2: classifying.go** — Add guard check in `processClassifyingTasks()`, inside the `for i := range tasks` loop, AFTER the human_triage skip (line 70) and BEFORE the `o.runner.CanSpawn()` check (line 73). Insert:

```go
// Budget guard: prevent runaway classifier spawns.
guard := &ClassifierBudgetGuard{}
if guard.Evaluate(task) == ClassifierFail {
    _ = o.parkClassifierForTriage(task, fmt.Sprintf(
        "classifier spawn cap reached for task %s", task.ID))
    continue
}
if err := o.db.Save(task).Error; err != nil {
    o.logger.Error("save classifier spawn count", "task_id", task.ID, "error", err)
    continue
}
```

Do NOT modify test files. Make the pre-written tests pass.
